# {{.Binary}}

A Go project laid out for the `go_bare_ddd1` profile: DDD in three layers over a
hand written foundation, with no framework.

    go mod tidy
    go build ./...
    go test ./...

`AGENTS.md` has the working instructions, including the checks that must pass
before a change is finished.

## Layout

| Path | What lives there |
| --- | --- |
| `foundation/` | The little of a framework this project has: subjects, permissions, repositories, HTTP and command line adapters. |
| `app/{{.Context}}/` | A bounded context. Domain model, ports and use cases, and nothing about storage or presentation. |
| `app/{{.Context}}/rest/`, `app/{{.Context}}/cli/` | Presentations. Each takes the use cases it calls. |
| `app/{{.Context}}/adapter/` | Implementations of the context's ports, named after the technology behind them. |
| `requirements/` | Requirements as Go values, and the source documents they cite. |
| `cmd/{{.Binary}}/` | The entry point, and the only place that names an adapter. |
